{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1402062-morpheus-sabinis-changeling-the-dreaming","id":1402062,"title":"\"Morpheus Sabinis\" Changeling The Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-10T06:54:32-07:00","id":1402062,"title":"\"Morpheus Sabinis\" Changeling The Dreaming","content":"In the book &quot;Nobles The Shining Host&quot; was there mentioned a practice made by Unseelie, most of the time, called &quot;Morpheus Sabinis&quot;, is it still possible at C20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T00:31:47-07:00","id":1402199,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they ignored it because they want to avoid any form of controversy that could splash back on them. Coincidentally I'm currently reading Shining Host for the first time.<br /> <br /> But as always keep whatever you want from older editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T16:33:17-07:00","id":1402324,"title":"","content":"It's not a special power or system or anything, it's just using Arts to take someone so far out of their own senses that the character can do whatever they want to the victim. Kind of like the ah... ahem, impregnation scene of &quot;Rosemary's Baby,&quot; I would guess.<br /> <br /> So, yes, it's still somethign that is possible to do, though it's the sort of thing that would get calling a time out at the table, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T16:00:43-07:00","id":1402877,"title":"","content":"I've used it in-game as therapy. Make a literal Memory Palace, lock each unwanted memory around an &quot;object&quot; in each room, lock, bar and bolt, the door behind you. Close the gates and it should hold until you Chrysalize again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T20:48:07-07:00","id":1403479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1402062-morpheus-sabinis-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1402877#post1402877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used it in-game as therapy. Make a literal Memory Palace, lock each unwanted memory around an &quot;object&quot; in each room, lock, bar and bolt, the door behind you. Close the gates and it should hold until you Chrysalize again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did not understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T23:09:33-07:00","id":1405476,"title":"","content":"A Memory Palace is a mnemonic device in real life. You use it to remember things. We made a literal one, and used it to contain and repress memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}